{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931824-so-you-want-to-be-an-exorcist","id":931824,"title":"So You Want To Be An Exorcist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T22:24:24-07:00","id":931824,"title":"So You Want To Be An Exorcist","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Here's a little guide on your options if you want to play some kind of exorcist in a Mortals or Mortals+ game. I'm making an assumption that you've read the Mortal Interactions part of the Ephemeral Beings rules.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Part 0 - It Takes A Certain Kind of Person</span></span><br /> Not everyone is cut out for kicking Ephemeral Beings out of the human world. There's a pretty short list of traits that will let you <i>easily</i> justify any of the merits and such you'll need.<br /> <br /> 1) You need to meditate - I don't care <i>how</i>, you just need to be someone who meditates. Prayer is a form of meditation, so keep that in mind.<br /> 2) A rock-solid mind. You <i>generally</i> want a high Integrity - there are ways around mind-breakage, but you're better off keeping that soul of yours nice and healthy.<br /> 3) An excuse to buy up Occult. Granted, <i>everyone</i> has one after you start meeting gribblies, but you want a <i>really</i> good excuse.<br /> 4) A Virtue that's generally applicable for Abjuration. Being Devout or Thorough is <i>incredibly</i>, <i>stupidly</i> useful here.<br /> <br /> So if &quot;exorcist&quot; doesn't fly as a character concept, the next best option is some kind of religious leader or occultist. I tend to prefer the religious leader, because it's <i>very</i> thematically appropriate, and it justifies some nice expansions to your character concept. Plus, there's going to be religious leaders <i>everywhere</i>, so you can fit them in pretty much any kind of Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Matter of Soul</span><br /> One <i>really</i>, <i>really</i> important thing to do is not lose your soul. Don't do it. Soul Loss <i>ruins</i> your ability to exorcist like chopping off someone's legs destroys their chances at being a marathon runner. There are ways around this, but they don't hold a candle to having a soul. Fortunately, you aren't at risk unless you voluntarily trade it away or you face some <i>nasty</i> supernatural mojo, so you're mostly safe unless your ST's a jerk or it's a big dramatic thing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Part 1 - The Hard Numbers</span><br /> You need certain kinds of hard numbers to be a good at this kind of thing. Luckily, they happen to be the kinds of stuff you were going to be picking <i>anyway</i>, so it's not that harsh.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attributes</span><br /> You want Resolve and Composure to both have <i>at least</i> three dots. Seriously. You are going to be rolling Resolve+Composure <i>so much</i>, it isn't even funny. On top of that, Intelligence and Wits need to have at least two dots - they're less vital, but you want that Intelligence for research and banishing, and that Wits for binding and warding.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Skills</span><br /> You have at least one dot in Occult. Note, this is <i>not</i> optional - if your schtick is exorcist, you've gotta know something about the stuff you're kicking around (Encyclopedic Knowledge is <i>cute</i>, but isn't going to replace actually knowing about Ghosts and such). I'd really advise starting with two to three dots in Occult, and to toss on some appropriate specialities. Other than Occult, taking Academics, Empathy, or Science at two dots gives you access to some <i>very</i> nice merits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Integrity</span><br /> Hoo boy, you want this to be no lower than a seven. You take a <i>large</i> penalty to Abjuration once you drop below that point - and all your other exorcist stuff takes those penalties too. Ideally, you want to have an effective Integrity of ten - then you have a +3 to Abjuration rolls, and can laugh off most Breaking Points. Luckily, the merits that help your exorcism stuff also tend to make your mind <i>rock hard</i>, so you won't have to worry about losing Integrity too much.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Part 2 - Your Options</span><br /> There are certain Merits that you <i>really, really</i> want if you want to protect mankind from stuff on the other side of Twilight. Here's a list - it's not <i>entirely</i> comprehensive, but it should cover most of it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Must Haves</span><br /> Basically, these merits are <i>central</i> to pulling off this concept mechanically. You can be an exorcist without them, but I wouldn't really suggest it.<br /> <br /> <b>Meditative Mind (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Meditative Mind \u2022\u2022 gives you +3 on all Resolve + Composure rolls you make in any day you meditate, and lets you ignore environmental penalties when meditating. This is <i>really, really nice</i> - this boosts all your Breaking Point and Abjuration rolls, as well as the rolls for a few other merits. If you decide to spring for a few more dots, Meditative Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 lets you successfully meditate with one success instead of four - speeds the whole process up.<br /> <br /> <b>Hardened Exorcist (\u2022\u2022)</b> [<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit#heading=h.4nug3g6xq3z9\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker</a>]<br /> If you can convince your ST that you should have this merit, do so. Adding your Occult (your favorite skill) to your Integrity for Abjuration purposes is <i>lovely</i>. If you can convince them, see if you can get further bonuses for having an effective Integrity <i>higher</i> than 10. The secondary benefit isn't going to show up so much, if you took my advice and picked an appropriate Virtue.<br /> <br /> <b>Patient (\u2022)</b><br /> It's so cheap, and so worth it - it gives you extra time to work with when you're trying to research or banish stuff.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nice Stuff</span><br /> These are nice to have, but aren't, strictly speaking, <i>must haves</i>. You'll appreciate having them, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Good Time Management (\u2022)</b><br /> If you have the dots in Academics or Science, you can grab this to cut down on the time investment for research, summoning, and meditating. It's useful if your games are frenetic enough that taking a few hours to hit a library isn't in the cards.<br /> <br /> <b>Esoteric Armory (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Personally, I don't really like this merit - it basically makes any subplot about getting your hands on a Bane completely superfluous. Still, not everyone wants to worry about that kind of thing, so it's here if you want it.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtuous (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Having two Virtues is useful, since you have backup if your first Virtue doesn't apply for some reason. And backups are good.<br /> <br /> <b>Professional Training (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> It was going to come up at some point - basically, any profession where you can justify Occult as an Asset Skill is a good one.<br /> <br /> <b>Library, Hobbyist Clique et al</b><br /> Does it give you a bonus to a Skill? Can that skill be Occult? Then you can probably wedge this kind of Merit in.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Turning On The Magic</span><br /> If you have access to Supernatural merits, you have a few more choices (ignore for a moment that Hardened Exorcist is <i>technically</i> a Supernatural merit). They also happen to be <i>interesting</i> than a lot of the more mundane merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Unseen Senses (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Yep. It's a classic, all right - pick the right variant, and you know when your chosen Ephemeral Being type is around. Really, really useful.<br /> <br /> <b>Medium (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> This is why you'd want Empathy 2+. It lets you talk to Ghosts and gives you the ability to summon (and kinda dismiss) Ephemeral Beings. Useful and thematic, so it'd be one of my first choices if supernatural merits are on the table.<br /> <br /> <b>Clear-Sighted (\u2022\u2022)</b> [V:tR Second Edition]<br /> This is tucked away in the appendix about the living. And it's <i>nice</i>. Spend one Willpower, and you're effectively immune to supernatural powers that fuck with your senses for the rest of the Scene. It's niche, but you can laugh off stuff like Hallucinate, which shouldn't be sneezed at.<br /> <br /> <b>Deadpan (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b> [M:tAw Second Edition]<br /> You need to be a Sleepwalker (which Hardened Exorcist <i>technically</i> does), but this merit makes you immune to supernaturally inflicted fear unless it plays off your Vice or a mental condition (in which case you just get a bonus). Helps you avoid being spooked by ghosts.<br /> <br /> <b>Bless Amulet (\u2022)</b> [<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit#heading=h.dhqdco670ba\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker</a>]<br /> The amulets this lets you make are great if you deal with a lot of Ephemeral Beings. It's a nice defense which can be handed around to other players or the poor victim you might be helping.<br /> <br /> <b>Consecrate Weapon (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b> [<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit#heading=h.pkp0caeoxv26\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker</a>]<br /> Honestly, I like this less than just finding out the Bane. But still, it's not like picking this up <i>hurts</i> you. Plus, you can use this with a pair of brass knuckles so you can punch spirits and such.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">To Tell The Truth (Wolf-Blooded)</span><br /> These merits are restricted to Wolf-Blooded (other than, technically, Tell) - they are some of the best merits for dealing with the ephemeral world, but bring quite a lot of baggage to the table. All these merits are in W:tF Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Tell [Piercing Eyes] (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> You can see everything in Twilight <i>all the time</i>. Forget Unseen Senses - you just plain <i>can see</i> the things you're trying to deal with.<br /> <br /> <b>Kamduis-Ur's Blood (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Of all the &quot;tribe&quot; merits, this one is probably the best for exorcism purposes. You get to make short-lived sigils that trap ghosts in one place, giving you some breathing room.<br /> <br /> <b>Gibbous Moon's Birth (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Take it for Occult, and don't look back. If you can have this, quietly ignore Hobbyist Clique.<br /> <br /> <b>Raised By Wolves (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> This makes you immune to Breaking Points from observing the supernatural. If you don't want to deal with actually rolling your <i>really big</i> pool for Breaking Points, you might as well pick this up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T22:26:39-07:00","id":931826,"title":"","content":"I might go through the minor templates from Hurt Locker and see if there's anything appropriate in there.<br /> <br /> By the way, you can easily get away with reliable 14-die dicepools for Abjuration as a starting character, while still leaving comfortable room for doing other stuff with your character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T22:49:43-07:00","id":931836,"title":"","content":"This is really cool. It kind of reminds me of character optimization guides I used to read on the old D&amp;D forums, but like... the CofD version. I'd love to see more guides like this, focused on different tasks or character concepts. Like one for building a Social Maneuvering expert, one for optimizing Perception-related rolls, etc.<br /> <br /> Reading this makes me want to play an exorcist character, which is always a good sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T00:34:00-07:00","id":931876,"title":"","content":"This is great! What's next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 07-15-2016, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T10:28:34-07:00","id":932076,"title":"","content":"Note that making super duper exorcist might be resources intesive, but making a merely &quot;efficient, good one&quot; isn't; this imho one of CofD strengths - you don't have to make your character solely devoted to one task to be good at something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T10:38:13-07:00","id":932083,"title":"","content":"Huh. Thanks. That's a ridiculously useful resource to have. I didn't even know Hurt Locker had the Hardened Exorcist merit before looking here. Certainly makes the job of making a Jakub W\u0119drowycz-style exorcist on starting char papers much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","user":"Inquisitor","date":". 07-15-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T11:06:53-07:00","id":932103,"title":"","content":"Question: Can Abjuration and such benefit from Teamwork rolls?<br /> <br /> Because I can almost see a group/team/squad of dedicated exorcists. Heh. The Exorcists, a [HBO, Netflix, whatever] series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T11:34:00-07:00","id":932116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931824-so-you-want-to-be-an-exorcist?p=932083#post932083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Thanks. That's a ridiculously useful resource to have. I didn't even know Hurt Locker had the Hardened Exorcist merit before looking here. Certainly makes the job of making a Jakub W\u0119drowycz-style exorcist on starting char papers much more useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, Hurt Locker isn't out yet, the referenced document is previewed a first draft. It's entirely possible that the Merit might not make the cut in the published version, or might work differently than it does in this draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:32:06-07:00","id":932174,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m thinking most of those merits would be equally useful for a necromancer or a summoner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:59:35-07:00","id":932192,"title":"","content":"To be fair there's very few situations where lower Attributes or Skills and less Merits are good for anything.<br /> <br /> Presumably if the thread is still around it will be updated when the Hurt Locker book comes up. It is reminiscent of the character optimization guides, which is something World of Darkness doesn't often need, as raising appropriate stats is often obvious. But the rules for Exorcism and abilities to help characters perform it are scattered around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:51:29-07:00","id":1088989,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hurt Locker Update</span><br /> <br /> OK, now that Hurt Locker has come out (OK, it came out a while ago), I thought I'd update this:<br /> <br /> <b>Bless Amulet:</b> It's gone from a one-dot merit to a one-to-three dot merit. If you grab all three dots, your amulets are permanent, so you might want to make some for all your friends.<br /> <b>Consecrate Weaponry:</b> Now you can deal Lethal to ephemeral beings in Twilight. It's a bit more worth it, but you'd still be better off finding the Bane.<br /> <b>Hardened Exorcist:</b> Is entirely unchanged - it's still <i>really</i> awesome.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> There probably won't be anything new until Geist or Hunter come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:36:19-07:00","id":1089139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931824-so-you-want-to-be-an-exorcist?p=1088989#post1088989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hurt Locker Update</span><br /> <br /> OK, now that Hurt Locker has come out (OK, it came out a while ago), I thought I'd update this:<br /> <br /> <b>Bless Amulet:</b> It's gone from a one-dot merit to a one-to-three dot merit. If you grab all three dots, your amulets are permanent, so you might want to make some for all your friends.<br /> <b>Consecrate Weaponry:</b> Now you can deal Lethal to ephemeral beings in Twilight. It's a bit more worth it, but you'd still be better off finding the Bane.<br /> <b>Hardened Exorcist:</b> Is entirely unchanged - it's still <i>really</i> awesome.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> There probably won't be anything new until Geist or Hunter come out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot Camera Obscura, which lets you go Fatal Frame on ephemeral beings. I don't think there's any mortal ability better for fighting ghosts and spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12712-tezof","name":"Tezof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:20:10-07:00","id":1089164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tezof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931824-so-you-want-to-be-an-exorcist?p=1089139#post1089139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You forgot Camera Obscura, which lets you go Fatal Frame on ephemeral beings. I don't think there's any mortal ability better for fighting ghosts and spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Camera Obscura is actually <i>terrible</i> by itself for the purposes of fighting ephemerals.<br /> <br /> \u2022 It only affects un-manifested ephemerals, and only deals Bashing. Compare pulling out the thing's Bane or a Consecrated Weapon, which are still useful if it manifests, and which deal Lethal to gribblies in Twilight.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Unless I'm reading it wrong, you have to spend the Willpower <i>every turn</i>. That's really darn expensive.<br /> <br /> \u2022 It gives the area you're fighting in the Open condition, which is <i>not good</i>. Compare, again, to Bane or Consecrated Weapon, which don't do that.<br /> <br /> The sole advantage is that you can use it to see Ephemerals in Twilight. You can get that for <i>much</i> cheaper by picking up the Piercing Eyes Tell, which <i>doesn't</i> cost nearly as much Willpower.<br /> <br /> I might put it in as a &quot;if you can't get the Piercing Eyes tell, you might want to consider this&quot;, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013